### Drill 2: Ingress Path Routing (`02-ingresses/`)

An `Ingress` operates at Layer 7 (HTTP/HTTPS) to route traffic to cluster services based on hostname headers and request
URI paths.

#### Prerequisite: Deploy Ingress-NGINX Controller

Standard `Ingress` resources require an active Ingress controller. Deploy the community Ingress-NGINX controller
(v4.15.1) via Helm:

```bash
cd /home/vagrant/cka/helm
./install-deprecated-nginx-ingress.sh
# Alias symlink: ./install-deprecated-ingress-nginx.sh
```

> [!WARNING]
> **NodePort Collision Notice**: Ingress-NGINX binds host/NodePort `30080` (HTTP) and `30443` (HTTPS). If NGINX Gateway
> Fabric is currently installed, uninstall it first (`helm uninstall ngf -n nginx-gateway`) to avoid port binding
> conflicts.

#### Step 1: Deploy Ingress Backend Services

```bash
cd {{ cka_lab_networking_dir }}/02-ingresses
cat cka-lab-ingress-backends.yaml
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-ingress-backends.yaml -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }}
kubectl rollout status deployment/cka-lab-ingress-web -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }} --timeout=60s
kubectl rollout status deployment/cka-lab-ingress-api -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }} --timeout=60s
```

#### Step 2: Generate and Apply Ingress Rules

In the CKA exam, rapidly scaffold Ingress resources using `kubectl create ingress`:

```bash
kubectl create ingress cka-lab-ingress \
  --class=nginx \
  --rule="{{ cka_lab_networking_domain | default('cka-lab.example.local') }}/web*=cka-lab-ingress-web-svc:80" \
  --rule="{{ cka_lab_networking_domain | default('cka-lab.example.local') }}/api*=cka-lab-ingress-api-svc:80" \
  --dry-run=client -o yaml
```

Apply the pre-staged Ingress resource with rewrite annotations:

```bash
cat cka-lab-ingress.yaml
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-ingress.yaml -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }}
kubectl get ingress cka-lab-ingress -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }}
kubectl describe ingress cka-lab-ingress -n {{ cka_lab_networking_namespace | default('default') }}
```

#### Step 3: Test L7 Path Routing with Host Headers

Probe the ingress endpoints by passing the virtual host header:

```bash
NODE_IP=$(kubectl get nodes -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.addresses[?(@.type=="InternalIP")].address}')

# Verify routing to Web backend (/web -> cka-lab-ingress-web-svc)
curl -i -H "Host: {{ cka_lab_networking_domain | default('cka-lab.example.local') }}" "http://${NODE_IP}:30080/web"

# Verify routing to API backend (/api -> cka-lab-ingress-api-svc)
curl -i -H "Host: {{ cka_lab_networking_domain | default('cka-lab.example.local') }}" "http://${NODE_IP}:30080/api"
```

#### Step 4: Run Automated Verification for Module 2

```bash
./test-ingress.sh
```

