## 4. Module 4: Kubernetes Network Policies & Hubble Triage

### Drill 4: Ingress & Egress Network Policies (`04-network-policies/`)

```bash
cd {{ cka_lab_networking_dir }}/04-network-policies
```

#### Step 1: Deploy Namespaces and Baseline Workloads

```bash
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-namespaces.yaml
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-backend-workload.yaml
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-client-workloads.yaml
```

Verify initial unrestricted connectivity:

```bash
kubectl exec -n {{ cka_lab_networking_client_namespace | default('cka-lab-net-client') }} cka-lab-client-authorized -- \
  wget -qO- -T 3 http://cka-lab-target-backend-svc.{{ cka_lab_networking_backend_namespace | default('cka-lab-net-backend') }}.svc.cluster.local:80
```

#### Step 2: Apply Default-Deny Ingress

```bash
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-default-deny-ingress.yaml
```

Now all inbound traffic to backend pods is dropped at the eBPF layer.

#### Step 3: Observe Drops with Cilium Hubble

In a separate terminal or background session, trace drops in real time:

```bash
hubble observe --namespace {{ cka_lab_networking_backend_namespace | default('cka-lab-net-backend') }} --verdict DROPPED -f
```

Attempting the `wget` connection will produce live `Policy denied (INGRESS)` events in Hubble.

#### Step 4: Allow Authorized Client & Egress DNS

```bash
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-allow-client-to-backend.yaml
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-egress-dns-policy.yaml
```

Authorized client (`access: authorized`) succeeds, while unauthorized client (`access: unauthorized`) is blocked.

#### Step 5: Killer.sh Q24 Egress Database Restriction

Apply fine-grained egress rules permitting traffic only to specific database ports:

```bash
kubectl apply -f cka-lab-egress-database.yaml
```

#### Step 6: Run Automated Verification for Module 4

```bash
./test-network-policies.sh
```

